{"slug":"how-this-blog-works","title":"How This Blog Works (and a Markdown Feature Tour)","date":"2026-10-20","updated":null,"description":"A tour of every Markdown feature this site supports: code blocks, terminal output, tables, callouts, images and captions. Doubles as a reference while writing.","category":"notes","platform":null,"difficulty":null,"tags":["meta","markdown"],"featured":true,"cover":null,"readingTime":2,"html":"<p>Every article on this site is a single Markdown file in the <code>content/</code> directory. The build validates its frontmatter, renders it to static HTML and adds it to the archive, the tag pages, the RSS feed, the sitemap and the search index. No React code is touched to publish a post.</p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-note\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Note</p>\n<p>This post is sample content that demonstrates the template. Keep it as a reference or delete it.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"the-pipeline\">The pipeline<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#the-pipeline\">#</a></h2>\n<figure><img src=\"/images/how-this-blog-works/content-pipeline.svg\" alt=\"How a Markdown file becomes a page\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>From a Markdown file to a static page on GitHub Pages.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A post is published when it has valid frontmatter and <code>published: true</code> (or no <code>published</code> field at all). Drafts with <code>published: false</code> are skipped entirely, so they never reach a page, the feed or the search index.</p>\n<h2 id=\"code-blocks\">Code blocks<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#code-blocks\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Fenced code blocks are highlighted at build time, so no highlighting script is shipped to readers. Every block has a copy button.</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">python</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"python\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> socket</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\"> grab_banner</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(host: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">str</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, port: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">int</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, timeout: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">float</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\"> 3.0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">) -> </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">str</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">    \"\"\"Connect to a TCP service and return the first bytes it sends.\"\"\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">    with</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> socket.create_connection((host, port), </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">timeout</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">timeout) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">as</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> s:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">        return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> s.recv(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">1024</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">).decode(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">errors</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"replace\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">).strip()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">print</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(grab_banner(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"10.10.10.10\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">22</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">))</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Terminal output works the same way, using <code>console</code> or <code>text</code> as the language:</p>\n<div class=\"code-block\"><div class=\"code-header\"><span class=\"code-lang\">console</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"copy-btn\" aria-label=\"Copy code to clipboard\" data-copy=\"\">Copy</button></div><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark-dimmed\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#adbac7;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#22272e\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"console\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">$ nmap -sC -sV -oN scans/initial 10.10.10.10</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">PORT   STATE SERVICE VERSION</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">22/tcp open  ssh     OpenSSH 8.9p1 Ubuntu</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF\">80/tcp open  http    nginx 1.18.0</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Inline code such as <code>sudo -l</code> is styled too.</p>\n<h2 id=\"tables\">Tables<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#tables\">#</a></h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>title</code></td><td>yes</td><td><code>\"Lantern Writeup\"</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>date</code></td><td>yes</td><td><code>\"2026-10-27\"</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>yes</td><td>20 to 300 characters</td></tr><tr><td><code>category</code></td><td>yes</td><td><code>writeup</code>, <code>research</code>, etc.</td></tr><tr><td><code>platform</code></td><td>no</td><td><code>HTB</code>, <code>THM</code>, <code>OffSec</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>tags</code></td><td>no</td><td><code>[linux, privesc]</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"callouts\">Callouts<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#callouts\">#</a></h2>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-tip\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Tip</p>\n<p>Write the description for someone skimming the archive. It is also used for search results and link previews.</p>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-warning\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Warning</p>\n<p>Never publish credentials, flags or details of systems you are not authorised to test.</p>\n</aside>\n<aside class=\"callout callout-caution\" role=\"note\"><p class=\"callout-title\">Caution</p>\n<p>Respect platform rules: many platforms ask that writeups of active machines stay unpublished until retirement.</p>\n</aside>\n<h2 id=\"headings-and-the-table-of-contents\">Headings and the table of contents<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#headings-and-the-table-of-contents\">#</a></h2>\n<p>Every <code>##</code> and <code>###</code> heading gets an anchor link and appears in the table of contents beside the article.</p>\n<h3 id=\"a-third-level-heading\">A third-level heading<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#a-third-level-heading\">#</a></h3>\n<p>Use these for sub-steps, such as \"Enumeration → Web\".</p>\n<h2 id=\"quotes\">Quotes<a class=\"heading-anchor\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" href=\"#quotes\">#</a></h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Plain blockquotes stay plain, for quoting documentation or advisories.</p>\n</blockquote>","toc":[{"depth":2,"id":"the-pipeline","text":"The pipeline"},{"depth":2,"id":"code-blocks","text":"Code blocks"},{"depth":2,"id":"tables","text":"Tables"},{"depth":2,"id":"callouts","text":"Callouts"},{"depth":2,"id":"headings-and-the-table-of-contents","text":"Headings and the table of contents"},{"depth":3,"id":"a-third-level-heading","text":"A third-level heading"},{"depth":2,"id":"quotes","text":"Quotes"}],"prev":{"slug":"jwt-algorithm-confusion","title":"JWT Algorithm Confusion: How It Happens and How to Prevent It"},"next":null,"related":[]}